                "span": 9
              },
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "lede",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "If you're researching a stainless steel dry van trailer, you're already thinking ahead about durability, longevity, and how your equipment holds up over time. But here's where most buyers pause: should you go with stainless steel or aluminum? It's not just a material question. It's a business decision that affects maintenance costs, fuel efficiency, and long-term ROI.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full",
                    "anchor": "post-lede"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-intro-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "At <a href=\"/locations/trailer-sales\">Sun State Trailers</a>, we work with owner-operators and fleet owners every day who are weighing these options. The goal is simple: to help you choose a trailer that works as hard as you do.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-why-material",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Why Material Matters in a Dry Van Trailer",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "why-material"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-why-material-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "A dry van trailer is built to handle consistent freight, long miles, and changing conditions. The material it's built from plays a major role in structural durability, weight and fuel efficiency, maintenance requirements, and overall lifespan. When you're comparing an aluminum vs steel dry van trailer, you're really comparing two different approaches to performance.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "co-why-material-2-row",
                  "type": "row",
                  "props": {
                    "gap": 0
                  },
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "id": "co-why-material-2",
                      "type": "column",
                      "props": {
                        "span": 12
                      },
                      "styles": {
                        "base": {
                          "borderWidth": 1,
                          "borderStyle": "solid",
                          "borderColor": "line",
                          "paddingTop": 26,
                          "paddingRight": 28,
                          "paddingBottom": 26,
                          "paddingLeft": 28,
                          "marginTop": 8,
                          "marginBottom": 34
                        }
                      },
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "id": "co-why-material-2-cta",
                          "type": "buttons",
                          "props": {
                            "align": "left",
                            "items": [
                              {
                                "ctaId": "browse-trailers",
                                "label": "See Dry Van Trailers We Have in Stock →"
                              }
                            ]
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-steel",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Stainless Steel Dry Van Trailer: Built for Strength",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "steel"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-steel-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "A stainless steel dry van trailer is known for its strength and resistance to damage. It's designed to handle tougher environments and heavier wear over time.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "cards-steel-2",
                  "type": "card-lists",
                  "props": {
                    "variant": "type",
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "title": "Benefits",
                        "points": [
                          {
                            "text": "<strong>High Durability:</strong> Handles impact and rough loading conditions well"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "<strong>Corrosion Resistance:</strong> Performs better in humid or coastal climates"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "<strong>Long Lifespan:</strong> Holds structural integrity over years of use"
                          }
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Tradeoffs to Consider",
                        "points": [
                          {
                            "text": "Heavier than aluminum"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Slightly lower fuel efficiency"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Higher upfront cost in some cases"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-steel-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "For Florida-based operators, this matters. Between heat, humidity, and coastal exposure, equipment takes a beating. Still, many operators see stainless steel as a long-term investment, especially for demanding routes.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "fig-1",
                  "type": "image",
                  "props": {
                    "width": "full",
                    "image": {
                      "src": "/img/blog/aluminum-vs-stainless-steel-dry-van-trailer/1.jpg",
                      "width": 1000,
                      "height": 667,
                      "alt": "Sun State team member checking a dry van trailer's rear door and panel construction"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-aluminum",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Aluminum Dry Van Trailer: Built for Efficiency",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "aluminum"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-aluminum-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Aluminum trailers are widely used across the industry, and for good reason.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "cards-aluminum-2",
                  "type": "card-lists",
                  "props": {
                    "variant": "type",
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "title": "Key Benefits",
                        "points": [
                          {
                            "text": "<strong>Lighter Weight:</strong> Improves fuel efficiency"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "<strong>Higher Payload Capacity:</strong> Carry more per load"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "<strong>Lower Upfront Cost</strong> in some cases"
                          }
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Tradeoffs to Consider",
                        "points": [
                          {
                            "text": "Less resistant to dents and impact"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "May require more frequent repairs in high-use environments"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Can wear faster under heavy-duty conditions"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-aluminum-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "For fleets focused on maximizing every mile, aluminum can be a strong option.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "co-aluminum-4-row",
                  "type": "row",
                  "props": {
